1
00:00:23,140 --> 00:00:25,495
( # Swing)

2
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,176
(Crowd cheering)

3
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:42,338
What are you doing?
We don't stop here.

4
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,376
(Whooping and yelling)

5
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:54,972
Get out of the car.

6
00:05:00,340 --> 00:05:02,092
(Tyres screeching)

7
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:07,813
(Yelling)

8
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,372
(Tyres screeching)

9
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:40,575
(Laughter)

10
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,458
(Laughter)

11
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:31,178
The boys found this on the floor
in the back of the Caddy.

12
00:08:31,260 --> 00:08:33,615
Yeah, they showed me.

13
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:38,012
Could be unrelated.

14
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,931
Could be.

15
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:43,774
Any of those dead kids
wearing pearl earrings?

16
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:49,378
No. Could be
someone's missing, maybe.

17
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,768
That's what I'm thinking.

18
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:25,219
(Door closing)

19
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,896
Just one more bag after that.

20
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:10,176
(Police siren )

21
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:15,216
I just wanted to come here.

22
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:19,891
- To Winkie's?
- This Winkie's.

23
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:22,933
OK.

24
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:25,250
Why this Winkie's?

25
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:30,696
It's kind of embarrassing.

26
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:35,172
Go ahead.

27
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,491
I had a dream about this place.

28
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:40,093
Oh, boy.

29
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:42,057
See what I mean?

30
00:11:43,580 --> 00:11:45,059
OK.

31
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:47,415
So you had a dream about this place.

32
00:11:48,620 --> 00:11:50,178
Tell me.

33
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:55,578
Well...

34
00:11:55,660 --> 00:11:57,218
(Clears throat)

35
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,211
It's the second one I've had.

36
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,256
But they're both the same.

37
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,170
They start out that I'm in here

38
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:08,013
but it's not day or night -

39
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:12,130
it's kind of half-night, you know?

40
00:12:12,220 --> 00:12:14,097
But it looks just like this.

41
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,136
Except for the light.

42
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:20,569
And I'm scared like I can't tell you.

43
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:27,009
Of all people,
you're standing right over there,

44
00:12:31,420 --> 00:12:33,376
by that counter.

45
00:12:35,540 --> 00:12:38,930
You're in both dreams
and you're scared.

46
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:44,298
I get even more frightened
when I see how afraid you are and...

47
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:50,255
then I realise what it is.

48
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:55,332
There's a man

49
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:58,257
in back of this place.

50
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:03,176
He's the one who's doing it.

51
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:07,290
I can see him through the wall.

52
00:13:07,380 --> 00:13:09,257
I can see his face.

53
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:20,132
I hope that I never see that face
ever outside of a dream.

54
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:32,531
That's it.

55
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:36,215
So, you came to see
if he's out there.

56
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:42,375
To get rid of this god-awful feeling.

57
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,612
Right, then.

58
00:14:32,340 --> 00:14:34,296
It's around here.

59
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:44,455
(Muffled, echoing)
Steve, you all right? Steve?!

60
00:15:44,540 --> 00:15:46,132
Steve?!

61
00:16:00,380 --> 00:16:02,735
(Telephone dialling)

62
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:09,212
(Ringing)

63
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:12,333
Hello?

64
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:16,540
The girl is still missing.

65
00:16:30,220 --> 00:16:32,176
(Ringing)

66
00:16:36,860 --> 00:16:38,452
Talk to me.

67
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:40,292
The same.

68
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:56,052
(Telephone )

69
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,213
Oh!

70
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,370
I can't believe it.

71
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:50,499
Well, it's time
to say goodbye, Betty.

72
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:53,174
It's been so nice
travelling with you.

73
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:55,569
Thank you, Irene, I was so nervous,

74
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:58,174
it was sure great
to have you to talk to.

75
00:17:58,260 --> 00:18:00,569
I'll watch for you on the big screen.

76
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:04,096
OK, Irene! Won't that be the day?

77
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:06,375
Good luck, Betty, dear.

78
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:09,452
Take care of yourself.
And be careful!

79
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,496
- I will.
- (Chuckles )

80
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:13,138
Thanks again.

81
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,496
It was so nice meeting you.
All the luck in the world.

82
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:18,252
Thank you.

83
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,331
- Bye.
- Bye!

84
00:18:27,020 --> 00:18:28,533
My bags!

85
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:30,053
Where to?

86
00:18:31,260 --> 00:18:33,251
1612 Havenhurst!

87
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:37,058
You got it.

88
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,610
Ten bucks says you're Betty.

89
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:56,089
Yes I am, Mrs Lenoix.

90
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:58,136
It is Mrs Lenoix, isn't it?

91
00:19:58,220 --> 00:20:00,415
In all my living glory, baby!

92
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,377
Pleased to meet you.

93
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,133
Just call me Coco,
everybody else does.

94
00:20:05,220 --> 00:20:08,212
- I'll go and get the key.
- OK, Coco!

95
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,489
Wilkins?! Wilkins!

96
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:19,493
If that damn dog craps
in the courtyard one more time

97
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:22,652
I'm gonna bake his little butt
for breakfast!

98
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:25,493
- You don't have any pets, do you?
- Oh, no.

99
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:28,936
Well, they're allowed,
I just don't like them.

100
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:33,810
There was a man that lived here once
that had a prize-fighting kangaroo.

101
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:38,769
You just wouldn't believe what that
kangaroo did to this courtyard.

102
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:43,416
Let's go see your aunt's apartment.
It's a good one.

103
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:45,456
I can hardly wait.

104
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:53,696
It's unbelievable!

105
00:20:53,780 --> 00:20:56,419
(Coco ) I told you.
(Betty ) Oh, wow!

106
00:20:57,660 --> 00:21:01,699
You and your aunt have
an understanding, so here's the key.

107
00:21:01,780 --> 00:21:04,294
- If you need anything, just holler.
- OK.

108
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:07,850
Everybody in this building
is pretty much OK with me

109
00:21:07,940 --> 00:21:10,135
- or they wouldn't be here.
- Mm.

110
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:13,371
If you like, later on,
I'll introduce you around.

111
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:16,133
Well, no hard feelings if you don't.

112
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:28,498
(Laughs )

113
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:42,698
Oh, my! I'm sorry, my aunt didn't
tell me anyone was gonna be here.

114
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:44,736
- I'm sorry!
- It's OK.

115
00:22:44,820 --> 00:22:50,053
I'm Ruth's niece. My name's Betty,
I'm sure she told you I was coming.

116
00:22:51,140 --> 00:22:53,973
There was an accident. I came here.

117
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:57,095
I understand. I saw the dress.

118
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:00,340
I'm sorry. Are you all right?

119
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,018
What happened?

120
00:23:04,540 --> 00:23:06,019
A car.

121
00:23:07,060 --> 00:23:09,130
A car accident.

122
00:23:09,220 --> 00:23:10,573
Oh.

123
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:12,298
Are you OK?

124
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:16,852
I think so.

125
00:23:17,820 --> 00:23:21,051
I was just...taking a shower.

126
00:23:22,020 --> 00:23:25,535
Oh, my God, I'm sorry.
I'll let you get back to that.

127
00:23:25,620 --> 00:23:28,054
I'm gonna get unpacked.

128
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:33,252
What's your name?

129
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:41,013
I'm...I'm sorry, I'll get out of here
and we can talk later.

130
00:24:16,700 --> 00:24:18,258
My name's...

131
00:24:18,340 --> 00:24:19,693
Rita.

132
00:24:19,780 --> 00:24:21,259
Hi.

133
00:24:22,420 --> 00:24:25,935
- Do you work with my aunt?
- No.

134
00:24:26,020 --> 00:24:28,693
- I...
- I'm sorry, it's...

135
00:24:28,780 --> 00:24:31,340
it's none of my business.

136
00:24:34,660 --> 00:24:36,776
She has pretty red hair.

137
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:40,978
She's letting me stay while
she's working on a movie in Canada

138
00:24:41,060 --> 00:24:43,210
but I guess you already know that.

139
00:24:43,300 --> 00:24:46,815
I couldn't afford a place like this
in a million years.

140
00:24:46,900 --> 00:24:50,688
Unless of course I'm discovered
and become a movie star.

141
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:53,453
I'd rather be known
as a great actress

142
00:24:53,540 --> 00:24:56,213
but sometimes people
end up being both.

143
00:24:56,300 --> 00:25:00,213
That is, I guess you'd say,
sort of why I came here.

144
00:25:03,740 --> 00:25:07,335
I'm sorry,
I'm just so excited to be here.

145
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:10,218
I mean, I just came here
from Deep River, Ontario

146
00:25:10,300 --> 00:25:12,211
and now I'm in this...

147
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:14,291
dream place!

148
00:25:14,380 --> 00:25:16,974
Well, you can imagine how I feel.

149
00:25:21,780 --> 00:25:23,213
Oh.

150
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:26,413
Sit down.

151
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:32,176
Where were you hurt?

152
00:25:34,700 --> 00:25:37,055
- Oh, we should call a doctor.
- No.

153
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:40,974
- But this could be serious.
- No, I...I need to sleep.

154
00:25:41,060 --> 00:25:43,733
If you have a concussion
you shouldn't sleep.

155
00:25:43,820 --> 00:25:45,970
I'll be OK if I sleep.

156
00:25:46,060 --> 00:25:49,097
I just need to lie down here
and sleep.

157
00:26:44,020 --> 00:26:45,931
You see, Adam,

158
00:26:46,020 --> 00:26:49,979
there are some suggestions
that are to be brought forward.

159
00:26:50,060 --> 00:26:53,450
I know you said you would
entertain suggestions

160
00:26:53,540 --> 00:26:56,691
and that's all anybody here
is asking you to do.

161
00:26:56,780 --> 00:26:58,930
What are you talking about?

162
00:26:59,700 --> 00:27:01,452
An open mind.

163
00:27:01,540 --> 00:27:05,089
You're in the process
of recasting your lead actress

164
00:27:05,180 --> 00:27:07,330
and I'm...

165
00:27:07,420 --> 00:27:10,969
We're asking you
to keep an open mind.

166
00:27:21,100 --> 00:27:23,250
What was it last time?

167
00:27:25,180 --> 00:27:27,614
OK, let's try the next one.

168
00:27:27,700 --> 00:27:29,930
He's not gonna like it.

169
00:27:30,020 --> 00:27:31,772
We'll see.

170
00:27:35,140 --> 00:27:37,096
(Door opens )

171
00:27:37,180 --> 00:27:41,332
(Laughs nervously)
The Castigliane brothers.

172
00:27:41,420 --> 00:27:43,411
Let me introduce you around.

173
00:27:44,500 --> 00:27:48,049
Oh, please... Er, just take a seat.

174
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:50,256
This is Mr Darby, who you know,

175
00:27:50,340 --> 00:27:53,491
and this is the director,
Adam Kesher

176
00:27:53,580 --> 00:27:56,697
and his manager, Robert Smith.

177
00:28:28,060 --> 00:28:29,539
Oh.

178
00:28:30,620 --> 00:28:32,975
- She's very pretty.
- Mm.

179
00:28:33,060 --> 00:28:36,575
May I offer you gentlemen...anything?

180
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:41,251
- Espresso.
- Nothing.

181
00:28:41,340 --> 00:28:43,535
Er...what's the photo for?

182
00:28:43,620 --> 00:28:45,417
(Darby ) One espresso.

183
00:28:46,500 --> 00:28:48,058
No, that's it.

184
00:28:48,140 --> 00:28:51,371
I think you're going to enjoy
your espresso this time.

185
00:28:51,460 --> 00:28:54,930
I've done research,
knowing how hard you are to please.

186
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:57,488
This one comes highly recommended.

187
00:28:57,580 --> 00:28:59,571
What's the photo for?

188
00:28:59,660 --> 00:29:01,730
It's a recommendation.

189
00:29:01,820 --> 00:29:05,415
(Older man ) 'A recommendation
to you, Adam.'

190
00:29:06,540 --> 00:29:09,850
- It's not a recommendation.
- This is the girl.

191
00:29:09,940 --> 00:29:12,170
What girl? For what?

192
00:29:12,260 --> 00:29:14,251
What is this, Ray?

193
00:29:14,340 --> 00:29:17,776
Uh, we'd be happy to put her up
for consideration.

194
00:29:17,860 --> 00:29:19,851
You'll be pleased to know

195
00:29:19,940 --> 00:29:23,057
that there's quite a bit
of interest in this role.

196
00:29:23,140 --> 00:29:25,700
Interest? No, no.

197
00:29:25,780 --> 00:29:28,169
Six of the top actresses want this.

198
00:29:28,260 --> 00:29:30,535
This is the girl.

199
00:29:30,620 --> 00:29:33,498
- Ray, take care of this.
- Hold on, Adam.

200
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:36,936
Hold on? There's no way.
There's no way!

201
00:29:54,940 --> 00:29:56,498
Pardon me?

202
00:29:56,580 --> 00:29:58,457
A napkin.

203
00:29:58,540 --> 00:30:00,132
Of course.

204
00:30:00,220 --> 00:30:01,778
Excuse me.

205
00:30:18,740 --> 00:30:20,537
Is that all, sir?

206
00:30:33,020 --> 00:30:34,578
(Door closes )

207
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:19,931
- (Coffee man ) Shit.
- That was a highly recommended...

208
00:31:20,020 --> 00:31:24,138
- One of the finest espressos!
- What is going on?

209
00:31:24,220 --> 00:31:27,769
- That girl is not in my movie.
- (Yells incoherently)

210
00:31:28,620 --> 00:31:32,898
- This is the girl.
- Hey! That girl is not in my film!

211
00:31:36,220 --> 00:31:38,609
It's no longer your film.

212
00:31:43,540 --> 00:31:45,292
This is the girl.

213
00:31:54,060 --> 00:31:55,539
Come on.

214
00:31:57,780 --> 00:31:59,736
(Door closes )

215
00:32:21,780 --> 00:32:25,659
Castigliane brothers
get out of that limo?

216
00:32:25,740 --> 00:32:28,129
- Two guys in dark suits?
- Yeah.

217
00:32:28,220 --> 00:32:30,973
- Yes.
- Keep that door open.

218
00:32:40,340 --> 00:32:43,810
- Castigliane brothers?
- (Man ) Beat it, pal.

219
00:32:44,700 --> 00:32:45,849
OK.

220
00:33:27,220 --> 00:33:29,097
Good afternoon, Mr Roque.

221
00:33:31,260 --> 00:33:34,013
'Her name is Camilla Rhodes.

222
00:33:34,100 --> 00:33:37,012
'The director doesn't want her.'

223
00:33:40,860 --> 00:33:42,896
Do you want him replaced?

224
00:33:45,420 --> 00:33:47,570
'I know they said...'

225
00:33:50,020 --> 00:33:51,692
Then...

226
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:54,055
'Then...'

227
00:33:54,140 --> 00:33:55,971
That means we should...

228
00:33:59,940 --> 00:34:01,498
Yes?

229
00:34:02,580 --> 00:34:04,536
'Shut everything down.

230
00:34:04,620 --> 00:34:06,975
'Is that something that...?'

231
00:34:08,060 --> 00:34:12,736
You...want us...
to shut everything down?

232
00:34:17,860 --> 00:34:20,374
Then we'll...shut everything down.

233
00:34:48,100 --> 00:34:49,852
Oh, man!

234
00:34:49,940 --> 00:34:52,295
- That's unheard of!
- (Laughing)

235
00:34:52,380 --> 00:34:55,929
An accident like that?
Who could have foreseen that?

236
00:34:56,020 --> 00:34:57,976
(Laughing)

237
00:34:58,060 --> 00:35:00,654
- It's unreal, right?
- Oh, yeah.

238
00:35:02,460 --> 00:35:04,212
Unbelievable, man.

239
00:35:04,300 --> 00:35:06,495
(Chuckling)

240
00:35:06,580 --> 00:35:08,332
Oh... Whoo!

241
00:35:10,660 --> 00:35:13,128
So, bro... God, you look good.

242
00:35:13,220 --> 00:35:15,017
What have you been doing?

243
00:35:15,100 --> 00:35:18,331
Oh, you know,
just doin' some stuff for this guy.

244
00:35:18,420 --> 00:35:20,376
Yeah? You making ends meet?

245
00:35:20,460 --> 00:35:22,052
Hardly.

246
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:27,455
(Sighs ) I know, man. Look at my digs.

247
00:35:29,420 --> 00:35:32,378
Times are tough, bro.

248
00:35:32,460 --> 00:35:34,928
Hey, man, it's not that bad.

249
00:35:35,980 --> 00:35:38,813
I hope you're not gonna get
in any trouble.

250
00:35:38,900 --> 00:35:42,734
Oh, that was just a thing, man,
but that story made you laugh.

251
00:35:42,820 --> 00:35:46,096
- That was a funny story.
- Fucking car accident!

252
00:35:49,500 --> 00:35:51,934
Hey, so that's...that's it, huh?

253
00:35:52,020 --> 00:35:54,898
That's Ed's famous black book.

254
00:35:57,540 --> 00:35:59,496
The history of the world

255
00:35:59,580 --> 00:36:01,571
in phone numbers.

256
00:36:22,020 --> 00:36:24,580
(Gunshot, woman yelling)

257
00:36:24,660 --> 00:36:26,378
Um...

258
00:36:28,060 --> 00:36:30,415
(Woman groaning)

259
00:36:30,500 --> 00:36:32,058
Oh, man!

260
00:36:44,380 --> 00:36:46,257
Somethin' bit me, bad!

261
00:36:46,340 --> 00:36:48,490
(Groaning)

262
00:36:50,780 --> 00:36:52,532
(Muffled screaming)

263
00:36:55,740 --> 00:36:57,935
(Screams )

264
00:36:58,020 --> 00:36:59,453
(Grunts, yells)

265
00:37:00,220 --> 00:37:02,415
- (Gasps )
- (Screams )

266
00:37:03,900 --> 00:37:07,529
(Groaning, gasping)

267
00:37:07,620 --> 00:37:10,180
No! (Screaming)

268
00:37:12,660 --> 00:37:15,094
(Muffled) No! No!

269
00:37:18,700 --> 00:37:21,897
(Grunting) God! God! Oh!

270
00:37:24,700 --> 00:37:27,168
(Strangled yelling)

271
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:30,216
(Muffled) No! No!

272
00:37:34,740 --> 00:37:37,015
Hey, man, hey! She's hurt real bad!

273
00:37:37,100 --> 00:37:40,217
Could you come and call on the phone?
I need you!

274
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:44,657
I'm serious! You gotta come
in here and call the hospital!

275
00:37:45,740 --> 00:37:50,177
Come on, man! I'm serious!
I can't do everything by myself!

276
00:37:50,260 --> 00:37:52,899
(Muffled screaming)

277
00:37:59,780 --> 00:38:02,169
(Woman ) Oh! No!

278
00:38:02,260 --> 00:38:04,649
No! No! No!

279
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:10,573
Hey, man.

280
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:14,292
(Hoover starts up )

281
00:38:42,300 --> 00:38:44,018
Um...

282
00:38:46,740 --> 00:38:49,493
(Alarm screeching)

283
00:38:50,580 --> 00:38:52,218
Oh, man...

284
00:39:08,300 --> 00:39:10,530
OK, Aunt Ruth, I'll try.

285
00:39:10,620 --> 00:39:14,852
I'm gonna study those lines
until I know 'em inside out.

286
00:39:14,940 --> 00:39:18,569
Yep, either right here
on this fabulous leather couch

287
00:39:18,660 --> 00:39:23,336
or I'll take them with a coffee
into the courtyard like a movie star.

288
00:39:23,420 --> 00:39:26,810
Oh, I got a real shock
to find your friend Rita here.

289
00:39:26,900 --> 00:39:29,778
She was in the shower
and I opened the door!

290
00:39:29,860 --> 00:39:31,213
Rita.

291
00:39:31,300 --> 00:39:33,131
What do you mean?

292
00:39:34,420 --> 00:39:36,411
Well, she was in an accident.

293
00:39:37,740 --> 00:39:39,093
Rita.

294
00:39:39,180 --> 00:39:40,738
Your friend.

295
00:39:41,820 --> 00:39:43,776
No, Coco unlocked the door.

296
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:47,212
No, she didn't see her.

297
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:49,938
She's sleeping.

298
00:39:50,020 --> 00:39:54,969
I'm sure there's some explanation,
I don't think we have to do that.

299
00:39:58,220 --> 00:40:01,371
Please don't worry.
We won't need the police.

300
00:40:14,780 --> 00:40:16,293
You're awake.

301
00:40:20,100 --> 00:40:22,534
I think I misunderstood.

302
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:26,010
I thought you knew my aunt
and that's why you were here.

303
00:40:26,100 --> 00:40:29,570
I just talked to my aunt
and she wants to call the police.

304
00:40:32,980 --> 00:40:34,538
(Sobbing)

305
00:40:35,420 --> 00:40:36,853
Rita?

306
00:40:40,620 --> 00:40:42,451
I'm sorry. I...

307
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:44,292
What is it, Rita?

308
00:40:48,420 --> 00:40:52,493
I thought when I woke up...
I thought sleep would do it.

309
00:40:53,740 --> 00:40:55,253
What's wrong?

310
00:40:57,500 --> 00:41:00,219
I...don't know who I am.

311
00:41:00,300 --> 00:41:02,450
What do you mean? You're Rita.

312
00:41:02,540 --> 00:41:06,499
No, I'm not.
I don't know what my name is.

313
00:41:06,580 --> 00:41:08,775
I don't know who I am.

314
00:41:19,100 --> 00:41:22,729
This is your purse.
Your name must be in your purse.

315
00:41:24,740 --> 00:41:27,095
You wanna know, don't you?

316
00:41:27,180 --> 00:41:30,252
- Yes, but...
- Open it.

317
00:43:01,140 --> 00:43:05,099
- Sure you don't want anything?
- Not here. No, thanks.

318
00:43:05,180 --> 00:43:07,410
- A drink or something?
- No.

319
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:09,058
Thanks, though.

320
00:43:09,140 --> 00:43:11,893
I'll take a cigarette,
if you have one.

321
00:43:14,380 --> 00:43:16,894
Just reach inside my shirt pocket.

322
00:43:22,060 --> 00:43:24,335
Any new girls on the street lately?

323
00:43:26,380 --> 00:43:27,733
No.

324
00:43:27,820 --> 00:43:29,538
Haven't seen any.

325
00:43:31,700 --> 00:43:33,258
A brunette?

326
00:43:33,340 --> 00:43:35,171
Probably a little beat-up.

327
00:43:36,620 --> 00:43:37,973
No.

328
00:43:42,020 --> 00:43:44,409
You keep your eyes open for me, baby.

329
00:43:44,500 --> 00:43:45,853
Sure.

330
00:43:45,940 --> 00:43:47,896
Yeah, you bet you will.

331
00:43:50,380 --> 00:43:52,336
That money...

332
00:43:54,100 --> 00:43:56,295
you don't know where it came from?

333
00:43:56,380 --> 00:43:58,052
Uh-uh.

334
00:43:59,620 --> 00:44:03,374
When you think of them,
the money and the key,

335
00:44:05,860 --> 00:44:08,454
does it make you remember anything?

336
00:44:10,820 --> 00:44:12,811
There is something...

337
00:44:14,260 --> 00:44:15,613
Something...

338
00:44:16,460 --> 00:44:18,416
there. I...

339
00:44:28,980 --> 00:44:32,450
- What did you say?
- (Woman ) 'They fired everyone.'

340
00:44:32,540 --> 00:44:34,258
Who fired everyone?

341
00:44:34,340 --> 00:44:38,094
'Ray did. Wait,
I'm talking on the phone.

342
00:44:38,180 --> 00:44:41,490
'And then they closed the set
and everybody's gone.

343
00:44:41,580 --> 00:44:43,969
'You'd better get down here, Adam.'

344
00:44:45,060 --> 00:44:46,379
No.

345
00:44:46,460 --> 00:44:49,133
'You've got to talk to Ray.
You've gotta fix this.'

346
00:44:49,220 --> 00:44:51,529
- I'm going home.
- 'Home?!

347
00:44:51,620 --> 00:44:55,693
'Meet me at the office,
we've gotta do something, Adam!'

348
00:44:55,780 --> 00:44:57,736
I'm going home, Cynthia.

349
00:44:57,820 --> 00:45:00,095
'Adam, this...this isn't like you.

350
00:45:00,180 --> 00:45:03,172
'Please, there must be
something we can do.'

351
00:45:03,260 --> 00:45:04,693
I'm going home.

352
00:45:15,220 --> 00:45:17,211
I wonder where you were going.

353
00:45:21,900 --> 00:45:23,652
Mulholland Drive.

354
00:45:29,020 --> 00:45:30,897
Mulholland Drive?

355
00:45:32,820 --> 00:45:35,129
That's where I was going...

356
00:45:35,220 --> 00:45:37,256
Mulholland Drive.

357
00:45:39,260 --> 00:45:41,820
Maybe that's where the accident was.

358
00:45:42,900 --> 00:45:45,892
There must be a police report -
we could call.

359
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:48,414
- No!
- We could call anonymously

360
00:45:48,500 --> 00:45:50,650
to see if there was an accident.

361
00:45:50,740 --> 00:45:53,573
Come on, it'll be
just like in the movies.

362
00:45:53,660 --> 00:45:56,015
We'll pretend to be someone else.

363
00:45:57,620 --> 00:45:59,531
I wanna walk around anyway,

364
00:45:59,620 --> 00:46:02,737
I'm in Hollywood
and I haven't seen any of it.

365
00:46:02,820 --> 00:46:05,209
Come on, Rita, do you feel up to it?

366
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:14,373
OK.

367
00:46:15,220 --> 00:46:17,211
But just...

368
00:46:18,820 --> 00:46:20,538
just to see.

369
00:46:21,620 --> 00:46:24,578
Just to see...
if there was an accident...

370
00:46:25,660 --> 00:46:27,412
on Mulholland Drive.

371
00:47:09,020 --> 00:47:10,453
Lorraine?

372
00:47:11,540 --> 00:47:13,292
Lorraine, you home?

373
00:47:16,580 --> 00:47:18,059
Lorraine!

374
00:47:38,100 --> 00:47:40,056
Now you've done it!

375
00:47:41,540 --> 00:47:45,453
Just forget you ever saw it.
It's better that way.

376
00:47:48,100 --> 00:47:51,012
What the hell are you
even doing here?!

377
00:48:02,380 --> 00:48:04,132
What are you doing?

378
00:48:07,780 --> 00:48:09,930
That's my jewellery!

379
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:28,459
That bastard. You bastard!

380
00:48:28,540 --> 00:48:30,656
He's probably upset, Lorraine.

381
00:48:36,820 --> 00:48:38,538
What are you doing?!

382
00:48:40,860 --> 00:48:43,977
Stop it! Stop it!

383
00:48:44,060 --> 00:48:46,130
Adam, stop it!

384
00:48:46,220 --> 00:48:49,371
(Sobbing) Stop it. Stop it!

385
00:48:53,780 --> 00:48:55,691
(Wailing) Gene!

386
00:48:55,780 --> 00:48:57,850
You're hurting me!

387
00:49:01,220 --> 00:49:05,179
That ain't no way to treat your
wife, I don't care what she's done.

388
00:49:06,060 --> 00:49:07,937
Throw him out!

389
00:49:08,740 --> 00:49:10,378
Throw him out!

390
00:49:11,140 --> 00:49:12,698
Damn you, Adam!

391
00:49:12,780 --> 00:49:14,975
Throw him out!

392
00:49:21,420 --> 00:49:23,411
Get out!

393
00:49:42,620 --> 00:49:44,338
(Engine starts )

394
00:50:00,660 --> 00:50:02,412
Let's hide it.

395
00:50:45,860 --> 00:50:47,816
There's one.

396
00:51:00,700 --> 00:51:03,168
(Ringing tone )

397
00:51:03,260 --> 00:51:05,137
'Hollywood Police Department.'

398
00:51:05,220 --> 00:51:08,690
I'm inquiring about an accident
last night on Mulholland Drive.

399
00:51:08,780 --> 00:51:11,613
'Hold, please,
I'll connect you to Traffic.'

400
00:51:12,700 --> 00:51:16,375
- 'Sergeant Baxter.'
- Hi, I'm enquiring...

401
00:51:18,140 --> 00:51:21,974
Well, I heard a sound last night
that was sorta like a car crash

402
00:51:22,060 --> 00:51:25,689
and I wanna know if there was
an accident on Mulholland Drive.

403
00:51:25,780 --> 00:51:29,136
- 'Yes, there was.'
- Can you tell me what happened?

404
00:51:29,220 --> 00:51:31,939
- 'No, I can't.'
- Was anyone hurt?

405
00:51:32,020 --> 00:51:34,409
'May I have your name, please?'

406
00:51:39,540 --> 00:51:41,496
There was an accident.

407
00:51:42,220 --> 00:51:46,498
He wouldn't tell me anything else
but that was your accident, I'm sure.

408
00:51:46,580 --> 00:51:49,936
(Sighs ) Maybe there's something
about it in the papers.

409
00:51:50,020 --> 00:51:52,250
I'll buy you a coffee and we can see.

410
00:51:55,380 --> 00:51:58,656
Maybe it happened so late
it's not in today's paper.

411
00:51:58,740 --> 00:52:00,458
There's nothing?

412
00:52:02,700 --> 00:52:04,656
Not that I can see.

413
00:52:06,700 --> 00:52:08,418
That's OK.

414
00:52:12,220 --> 00:52:13,778
Thanks.

415
00:52:15,260 --> 00:52:16,932
Diane.

416
00:52:21,500 --> 00:52:24,890
Will that be all?
Would you like your check?

417
00:52:24,980 --> 00:52:26,732
Rita, you want something?

418
00:52:29,580 --> 00:52:31,696
No, just...just the coffee.

419
00:52:31,780 --> 00:52:34,817
- We'll take our check.
- OK.

420
00:52:39,940 --> 00:52:42,454
- What is it, Rita?
- Shh.

421
00:52:49,820 --> 00:52:51,776
I remember something.

422
00:52:52,780 --> 00:52:54,930
I remember something!

423
00:52:57,020 --> 00:52:58,931
What is it?

424
00:52:59,020 --> 00:53:02,490
Diane Selwyn - maybe that's my name.

425
00:53:08,580 --> 00:53:10,855
D Selwyn. It's the only one.

426
00:53:12,420 --> 00:53:14,376
I'm gonna call.

427
00:53:21,060 --> 00:53:23,654
It's strange to be calling yourself.

428
00:53:23,740 --> 00:53:25,696
Maybe it's not me.

429
00:53:25,780 --> 00:53:28,613
(Ringing tone )

430
00:53:33,700 --> 00:53:36,772
'Hello, it's me. Leave a message.'

431
00:53:39,860 --> 00:53:41,816
That's not my voice.

432
00:53:42,900 --> 00:53:44,936
But I know her.

433
00:53:46,940 --> 00:53:49,898
Maybe that isn't
Diane Selwyn's voice.

434
00:53:49,980 --> 00:53:51,936
Maybe that's your roommate.

435
00:53:52,780 --> 00:53:54,736
Or, if it is Diane Selwyn,

436
00:53:54,820 --> 00:53:56,811
she could tell you who you are.

437
00:53:57,900 --> 00:53:59,458
Maybe.

438
00:54:00,460 --> 00:54:02,416
Maybe, maybe.

439
00:54:06,500 --> 00:54:09,333
# Baby

440
00:54:15,020 --> 00:54:17,818
# Baby

441
00:54:22,820 --> 00:54:26,176
- # I'm gonna bring it on home to you
- (Doorbell)

442
00:54:26,980 --> 00:54:29,175
# I done bought my ticket

443
00:54:29,660 --> 00:54:31,616
# I got my load... #

444
00:54:35,300 --> 00:54:37,131
Adam Kesher?

445
00:54:39,620 --> 00:54:42,373
- Adam Kesher!
- Get lost!

446
00:54:42,460 --> 00:54:45,736
- This is Adam Kesher's house.
- Like hell it is! Get out now!

447
00:54:45,820 --> 00:54:47,776
Get out!

448
00:54:48,540 --> 00:54:51,293
- (Shrieking)
- Adam Kesher?

449
00:54:55,660 --> 00:54:59,175
Get out of here!
He's never coming back! Ever!

450
00:55:01,140 --> 00:55:05,418
Don't you understand English?
She said leave. Here's the door.

451
00:55:05,500 --> 00:55:07,013
Gene!

452
00:55:07,100 --> 00:55:09,614
Get out!

453
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:12,692
- Get out!
- # Baby... #

454
00:55:14,500 --> 00:55:16,456
Adam Kesher?

455
00:55:29,820 --> 00:55:31,890
(Knocks )

456
00:55:38,180 --> 00:55:40,136
Yeah, what is it, Cookie?

457
00:55:40,220 --> 00:55:44,975
Sorry, Mr Kesher, but there seems to
be a problem with your credit cards.

458
00:55:45,060 --> 00:55:47,699
What? I pay you cash, Cookie.

459
00:55:49,460 --> 00:55:52,736
Yes, uh...two guys
from your bank came by.

460
00:55:53,660 --> 00:55:55,412
My bank?

461
00:55:56,500 --> 00:55:58,536
How did they know I was here?

462
00:55:58,620 --> 00:56:00,372
I don't know.

463
00:56:00,460 --> 00:56:02,416
What did they say?

464
00:56:02,500 --> 00:56:06,175
I'm afraid they said to tell you
that you're maxed out at your bank

465
00:56:06,260 --> 00:56:09,889
and that your line of credit
has been cancelled.

466
00:56:10,980 --> 00:56:12,936
That's unbelievable.

467
00:56:13,020 --> 00:56:14,738
Uh...

468
00:56:14,820 --> 00:56:16,776
Well, look, uh...

469
00:56:18,860 --> 00:56:21,135
I don't know what's going on. Uh...

470
00:56:21,220 --> 00:56:23,336
That is so much baloney.

471
00:56:23,420 --> 00:56:25,376
(Both chuckle )

472
00:56:25,460 --> 00:56:28,418
Well, I got
enough cash for you, Cookie.

473
00:56:28,500 --> 00:56:30,536
Oh, I know, I know.

474
00:56:30,620 --> 00:56:32,372
Don't worry.

475
00:56:32,460 --> 00:56:34,416
But I'm sorry.

476
00:56:34,500 --> 00:56:36,809
It was my duty to inform you.

477
00:56:38,540 --> 00:56:40,496
You ain't got nothing now.

478
00:56:40,580 --> 00:56:44,368
Whoever you're hiding from,
they know where you are.

479
00:56:46,380 --> 00:56:47,972
Right.

480
00:56:49,060 --> 00:56:50,891
I'm sorry.

481
00:57:02,740 --> 00:57:04,696
(Dialling tone )

482
00:57:12,820 --> 00:57:15,254
- (Phone rings )
- Hello?

483
00:57:15,340 --> 00:57:17,296
Someone maybe shut off my money.

484
00:57:17,380 --> 00:57:19,336
'I know. Where are you, Adam?'

485
00:57:19,420 --> 00:57:21,331
What do you mean, you know?

486
00:57:21,420 --> 00:57:25,299
Somebody called and told me
you were as good as broke.

487
00:57:25,380 --> 00:57:27,769
I didn't believe them
so I made some calls.

488
00:57:27,860 --> 00:57:29,976
- And?
- 'You're broke.'

489
00:57:30,060 --> 00:57:34,372
- But I'm not broke.
- I know, but you are. Where are you?

490
00:57:35,460 --> 00:57:37,416
I'm at Cookie's, downtown.

491
00:57:37,500 --> 00:57:39,730
Do you know somebody called...

492
00:57:39,820 --> 00:57:42,015
the Cowboy?

493
00:57:42,100 --> 00:57:45,172
- The Cowboy?
- Yeah.

494
00:57:45,260 --> 00:57:49,811
The Cowboy. This guy, the Cowboy,
wants to see you.

495
00:57:49,900 --> 00:57:53,336
'Jason said he thought
it'd be a good idea.'

496
00:57:53,420 --> 00:57:56,969
Jason thought it'd be a good idea
for me to go see the Cowboy?

497
00:57:57,060 --> 00:58:00,211
Should I wear my ten-gallon hat
and my six-shooters?

498
00:58:00,300 --> 00:58:03,736
Something tells me that this guy
is connected to what's happening.

499
00:58:03,820 --> 00:58:07,779
'Adam, I think you should do it and
I think you should do it right away.'

500
00:58:07,860 --> 00:58:09,816
What's going on, Cynthia?

501
00:58:09,900 --> 00:58:12,573
'It's been a very strange day.'

502
00:58:13,940 --> 00:58:15,896
And getting stranger.

503
00:58:17,940 --> 00:58:21,899
So where do I meet this Cowboy?
Do I have to ride out to the range?

504
00:58:21,980 --> 00:58:23,936
Sort of, funny boy.

505
00:58:24,020 --> 00:58:26,898
If I tell him the meeting's on

506
00:58:26,980 --> 00:58:30,131
you'll have to go
to the top of Beechwood Canyon

507
00:58:30,220 --> 00:58:33,690
and there's a corral up there
where he'll be.

508
00:58:33,780 --> 00:58:35,736
Oh, you've gotta be kidding me.

509
00:58:35,820 --> 00:58:37,811
'Will you meet with him?'

510
00:58:37,900 --> 00:58:39,538
Yeah.

511
00:58:39,620 --> 00:58:42,339
Sure. No, it's been
that kind of a day.

512
00:58:42,420 --> 00:58:43,933
When?

513
00:58:44,020 --> 00:58:47,456
Um, I'll call him right away
and then I'll call you back.

514
00:58:48,580 --> 00:58:52,653
You know, you...you could stay
at my place if you...if you wanted.

515
00:58:52,740 --> 00:58:55,732
Uh, Cynthia, no, I don't think
that'd be a good idea.

516
00:58:55,820 --> 00:58:57,970
I was just offering a place to stay.

517
00:58:58,060 --> 00:59:01,211
Yes, and I appreciate it, Cynthia.
I'll find a place.

518
00:59:01,300 --> 00:59:04,497
Just go and give that Cowboy a yodel
and get on back to me.

519
00:59:04,580 --> 00:59:07,572
'OK. But you don't know
what you're missing.'

520
00:59:07,660 --> 00:59:11,016
Just...get along, little dogie,
and call me back.

521
00:59:22,020 --> 00:59:24,898
(Betty ) It's right about here -
Sierra Bonita.

522
00:59:24,980 --> 00:59:26,936
It's not too far away.

523
00:59:27,980 --> 00:59:29,936
What's wrong with that?

524
00:59:31,020 --> 00:59:32,976
I'm not sure about this.

525
00:59:34,420 --> 00:59:36,650
I know you're afraid of something.

526
00:59:37,900 --> 00:59:40,016
We'll be careful, I promise.

527
00:59:41,500 --> 00:59:44,139
Tomorrow we'll go over there.

528
00:59:44,220 --> 00:59:46,370
Then we'll find out.

529
00:59:49,980 --> 00:59:52,335
(Soft knocking on door)

530
00:59:59,420 --> 01:00:01,376
It'll be OK.

531
01:00:01,460 --> 01:00:03,496
(Knocking)

532
01:00:03,580 --> 01:00:05,536
It's probably Coco.

533
01:00:09,620 --> 01:00:11,736
Yes? May I help you?

534
01:00:11,820 --> 01:00:14,129
Someone is in trouble.

535
01:00:15,220 --> 01:00:17,176
Who are you?

536
01:00:18,260 --> 01:00:21,457
What are you doing
in Ruth's apartment?

537
01:00:21,540 --> 01:00:26,091
She's letting me stay here,
I'm her niece. My name's Betty.

538
01:00:26,180 --> 01:00:29,729
No, it's not.
That's not what she said.

539
01:00:30,460 --> 01:00:34,009
Someone is in trouble,
something bad is happening!

540
01:00:35,100 --> 01:00:38,376
Well, I'm sorry,
but I don't know who you are, and...

541
01:00:38,460 --> 01:00:41,133
Louise? What are you doing, Louise?

542
01:00:42,220 --> 01:00:45,849
Oh, Coco, I've been trying
to get a hold of you

543
01:00:45,940 --> 01:00:47,896
since three o'clock this afternoon.

544
01:00:47,980 --> 01:00:50,892
That one is in my room
and she won't leave.

545
01:00:50,980 --> 01:00:53,335
I want you to get her out now.

546
01:00:53,420 --> 01:00:56,651
This is Louise Bonner,
I'm sure she meant well.

547
01:00:56,740 --> 01:00:59,732
(Coco ) Louise, this is Betty,
this is Ruth's niece.

548
01:00:59,820 --> 01:01:03,335
In fact, fortunately I was
just on my way over to see Betty.

549
01:01:03,420 --> 01:01:05,376
Betty's a young actress

550
01:01:05,460 --> 01:01:09,499
and I was just delivering a fax of
a scene for a big audition tomorrow.

551
01:01:09,580 --> 01:01:12,140
- Well, here they are, honey.
- Thank you.

552
01:01:12,220 --> 01:01:14,780
Come along, Louise,
I'll take you home.

553
01:01:14,860 --> 01:01:16,816
I'm sorry, it happens sometimes.

554
01:01:16,900 --> 01:01:20,575
No. No, she said it was someone else
who was in trouble.

555
01:01:20,660 --> 01:01:24,096
Stop it, Louise, I'm taking you home.
Come on.

556
01:01:24,180 --> 01:01:27,013
- Good night, Betty.
- Good night.

557
01:01:28,060 --> 01:01:30,016
Good night.

558
01:01:39,580 --> 01:01:41,298
Whoa.

559
01:02:07,220 --> 01:02:10,292
Cowboy! (Chuckles )

560
01:02:58,420 --> 01:03:00,172
(Buzzing)

561
01:03:13,820 --> 01:03:17,096
- Howdy.
- Howdy to you.

562
01:03:19,500 --> 01:03:21,775
Beautiful evenin'.

563
01:03:21,860 --> 01:03:23,612
Yeah.

564
01:03:24,700 --> 01:03:28,375
Sure wanna thank you for
coming up here to see me from that...

565
01:03:28,460 --> 01:03:30,655
nice hotel downtown.

566
01:03:32,140 --> 01:03:35,098
No problem. What's on your mind?

567
01:03:35,180 --> 01:03:38,650
Well, now, here's a man
who wants to get right down to it.

568
01:03:38,740 --> 01:03:41,015
Kinda anxious to get to it, are ya?

569
01:03:42,260 --> 01:03:43,818
Whatever.

570
01:03:45,140 --> 01:03:47,096
A man's attitude...

571
01:03:47,180 --> 01:03:50,172
A man's attitude goes some ways

572
01:03:50,260 --> 01:03:52,296
to the way his life will be.

573
01:03:53,300 --> 01:03:56,098
Is that somethin'
you might agree with?

574
01:03:56,180 --> 01:03:57,818
Sure.

575
01:03:57,900 --> 01:04:02,291
Now, did you answer because that's
what you thought I wanted to hear

576
01:04:02,380 --> 01:04:04,575
or did you think about what I said

577
01:04:04,660 --> 01:04:08,016
and answer because
you truly believe that to be right?

578
01:04:09,100 --> 01:04:11,056
I agree with what you said.

579
01:04:11,940 --> 01:04:13,498
Truly.

580
01:04:15,100 --> 01:04:17,056
What did I say?

581
01:04:19,420 --> 01:04:23,379
That a man's attitude determines to
a large extent how his life will be.

582
01:04:24,460 --> 01:04:26,416
So since you agree,

583
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:29,536
you must be a person who does not...

584
01:04:29,620 --> 01:04:32,293
care about the good life.

585
01:04:32,380 --> 01:04:34,450
How's that?

586
01:04:35,540 --> 01:04:37,815
Well, stop for a little second

587
01:04:37,900 --> 01:04:39,856
and think about it.

588
01:04:39,940 --> 01:04:42,090
Can you do that for me?

589
01:04:42,180 --> 01:04:44,171
(Chuckles )

590
01:04:44,260 --> 01:04:46,216
OK. I'm thinking.

591
01:04:50,020 --> 01:04:51,976
No, you're not thinking.

592
01:04:52,060 --> 01:04:55,370
You're too busy being a smart aleck
to be thinking.

593
01:04:56,380 --> 01:04:58,336
Now, I want you to think

594
01:04:58,420 --> 01:05:00,376
and stop being a smart aleck.

595
01:05:00,460 --> 01:05:02,416
Can you try that for me?

596
01:05:03,380 --> 01:05:07,214
Look, where's this going?
Or what do you want me to do?

597
01:05:07,300 --> 01:05:09,256
There's sometimes a buggy.

598
01:05:10,340 --> 01:05:12,808
How many drivers does a buggy have?

599
01:05:12,900 --> 01:05:14,891
One.

600
01:05:14,980 --> 01:05:18,017
So let's just say
I'm drivin' this buggy

601
01:05:18,100 --> 01:05:20,455
and, if you fix your attitude,

602
01:05:20,540 --> 01:05:22,974
you can ride along with me.

603
01:05:23,060 --> 01:05:25,016
OK.

604
01:05:25,100 --> 01:05:27,898
I want you
to go back to work tomorrow.

605
01:05:27,980 --> 01:05:31,336
You were recasting
the lead actress anyway.

606
01:05:31,420 --> 01:05:34,332
Audition many girls for the part.

607
01:05:35,420 --> 01:05:40,175
When you see the girl that was shown
to you earlier today, you will say,

608
01:05:40,260 --> 01:05:42,535
"This is the girl."

609
01:05:43,500 --> 01:05:47,049
The rest of the cast can stay,
that's up to you.

610
01:05:48,580 --> 01:05:51,299
But that lead girl is not up to you.

611
01:05:52,380 --> 01:05:54,371
Now, you will see me

612
01:05:54,460 --> 01:05:56,928
one more time if you do good.

613
01:05:57,900 --> 01:06:00,539
You will see me two more times

614
01:06:01,580 --> 01:06:03,536
if you do bad.

615
01:06:03,620 --> 01:06:05,576
Good night.

616
01:06:29,540 --> 01:06:31,371
You're still here?

617
01:06:31,460 --> 01:06:34,133
I came back.
I thought that's what you wanted.

618
01:06:34,220 --> 01:06:36,051
Nobody wants you here.

619
01:06:36,140 --> 01:06:37,698
Really?

620
01:06:37,780 --> 01:06:41,090
My parents are right upstairs,
they think you've left.

621
01:06:41,180 --> 01:06:43,330
- So? Surprise.
- I can call them.

622
01:06:43,420 --> 01:06:45,376
I can call my dad.

623
01:06:45,460 --> 01:06:47,416
But you won't.

624
01:06:47,500 --> 01:06:51,129
If you're trying to blackmail me,
it's not gonna work.

625
01:06:51,220 --> 01:06:55,099
- You're playing a dangerous game.
- You know what I want.

626
01:06:55,180 --> 01:06:58,490
Get out.
Get out before I call my dad.

627
01:06:58,580 --> 01:07:01,219
He trusts you,
you're his best friend.

628
01:07:01,300 --> 01:07:04,098
This will be the end of everything.

629
01:07:04,180 --> 01:07:07,252
What about you?
What will your dad think about you?

630
01:07:07,340 --> 01:07:10,776
Stop! Just stop it! That's what
you said from the beginning.

631
01:07:10,860 --> 01:07:14,569
If I tell what happened, they'll
arrest you and put you in jail,

632
01:07:14,660 --> 01:07:17,333
so get out of here before...

633
01:07:17,420 --> 01:07:19,775
Bef...Before what?

634
01:07:19,860 --> 01:07:21,578
Before...

635
01:07:21,660 --> 01:07:23,491
I kill you.

636
01:07:23,580 --> 01:07:25,889
Then they'd put you in jail.

637
01:07:26,980 --> 01:07:28,857
(Laughs )

638
01:07:28,940 --> 01:07:31,500
Then I cry and cry and cry

639
01:07:31,580 --> 01:07:35,414
and then I say with big emotion,
"I hate you! I hate us both!"

640
01:07:35,500 --> 01:07:38,412
(Both giggle )

641
01:07:38,500 --> 01:07:42,129
- Such a lame scene.
- Oh, but you are really good.

642
01:07:43,340 --> 01:07:45,615
(Thespian accent) Thank you, darling.

643
01:07:58,980 --> 01:08:00,811
Hi, there.

644
01:08:00,900 --> 01:08:02,856
Who are you?

645
01:08:02,940 --> 01:08:04,498
Uh...

646
01:08:05,420 --> 01:08:07,092
Betty?

647
01:08:13,260 --> 01:08:16,252
Uh, Betty,
can I see you outside for a minute?

648
01:08:29,380 --> 01:08:31,336
What is it, Coco?

649
01:08:31,420 --> 01:08:33,376
Your aunt called.

650
01:08:34,540 --> 01:08:36,496
I was afraid of that.

651
01:08:36,580 --> 01:08:39,777
She wants to know
who's staying in her apartment.

652
01:08:39,860 --> 01:08:43,011
It's just for a night or two,
until she finds her own place.

653
01:08:43,100 --> 01:08:46,331
I tried to explain to Aunt Ruth
but the connection was bad

654
01:08:46,420 --> 01:08:48,376
and she got it all mixed up.

655
01:08:48,460 --> 01:08:52,976
I kept saying it was my friend Rita
and she said she didn't know a Rita!

656
01:08:54,060 --> 01:08:58,292
- Look at me straight, sweetie.
- Coco, she's very nice.

657
01:08:58,380 --> 01:09:00,336
Honey, you're a good kid

658
01:09:00,420 --> 01:09:03,332
but what you're telling me
is a load of horse pucky,

659
01:09:03,420 --> 01:09:06,059
even though
it comes from a good place.

660
01:09:06,140 --> 01:09:09,177
Now, I'm gonna trust you
to sort this thing out.

661
01:09:09,260 --> 01:09:12,491
- Thank you.
- Don't make me out to be a sucker.

662
01:09:12,580 --> 01:09:16,334
Louise Bonner said there's trouble
in there. Remember last night?

663
01:09:17,180 --> 01:09:19,694
Well, sometimes she's wrong

664
01:09:19,780 --> 01:09:21,975
but if there is trouble,

665
01:09:22,060 --> 01:09:24,210
get rid of it.

666
01:09:33,820 --> 01:09:37,893
Is everything all right?
Is it bad for you that I'm here?

667
01:09:37,980 --> 01:09:40,892
No, no, everything is A-OK.

668
01:09:40,980 --> 01:09:43,448
Now, I've gotta fix that sandwich.

669
01:09:43,540 --> 01:09:45,895
And my audition is in one hour!

670
01:09:45,980 --> 01:09:47,936
(Betty giggles )

671
01:10:05,460 --> 01:10:07,928
I hope I'm back in a couple of hours.

672
01:10:08,020 --> 01:10:11,092
- And don't drink all the Coke.
- Good luck!

673
01:10:11,180 --> 01:10:14,570
When I get back I'll keep
the cab waiting so be ready to go.

674
01:10:14,660 --> 01:10:16,969
- OK.
- OK.

675
01:10:41,460 --> 01:10:43,530
(Man chuckles )

676
01:10:43,620 --> 01:10:45,133
Voilà.

677
01:10:45,220 --> 01:10:47,017
Betty Elms,

678
01:10:47,100 --> 01:10:51,013
I would like you to meet
Jack Tutland, my assistant.

679
01:10:51,820 --> 01:10:56,211
Woody Katz, who is playing Chuck
and will do the scene with you.

680
01:10:57,700 --> 01:10:59,656
Bob Brooker, our director.

681
01:10:59,740 --> 01:11:02,334
And Julie Chadwick.

682
01:11:02,420 --> 01:11:04,809
Now, our surprise guest,

683
01:11:04,900 --> 01:11:06,970
Linney James.

684
01:11:07,060 --> 01:11:09,938
Alas, we can't afford her
to cast our show

685
01:11:10,020 --> 01:11:11,976
but, well, as casting agents go,

686
01:11:12,060 --> 01:11:14,016
she is the best.

687
01:11:14,100 --> 01:11:17,570
Why, thank you, Wally. Hello, Betty.

688
01:11:17,660 --> 01:11:19,457
Very pleased to meet you.

689
01:11:19,540 --> 01:11:21,656
This is my assistant, Nicki.

690
01:11:21,740 --> 01:11:23,059
Oh,

691
01:11:23,140 --> 01:11:25,290
and the ever lovely Martha.

692
01:11:25,380 --> 01:11:28,736
Martha Johnson,
whom you met at the front.

693
01:11:29,540 --> 01:11:31,815
- Hi.
- (Man laughs )

694
01:11:31,900 --> 01:11:34,619
So...shall we give it a go?

695
01:11:36,060 --> 01:11:39,609
Would you like
a water or coffee before we begin?

696
01:11:39,700 --> 01:11:41,656
No, I'm fine.

697
01:11:41,740 --> 01:11:44,698
Well, then,
let's everyone take a seat.

698
01:11:44,780 --> 01:11:46,930
(He chuckles )

699
01:11:47,020 --> 01:11:48,533
Betty,

700
01:11:48,620 --> 01:11:52,408
why don't you join Woody over there
and we'll play the scene?

701
01:11:52,500 --> 01:11:54,013
Bob,

702
01:11:54,100 --> 01:11:56,819
do you have anything you wish to say?

703
01:11:56,900 --> 01:11:59,209
Something to Betty before we begin?

704
01:11:59,300 --> 01:12:00,653
No.

705
01:12:00,740 --> 01:12:02,412
It's not a contest.

706
01:12:03,500 --> 01:12:05,456
The two of them,

707
01:12:05,540 --> 01:12:07,610
with themselves.

708
01:12:09,180 --> 01:12:12,058
So don't play it for real...

709
01:12:13,020 --> 01:12:15,898
until it gets real.

710
01:12:20,460 --> 01:12:22,178
OK.

711
01:12:22,260 --> 01:12:24,376
Just tell me where it hurts, baby.

712
01:12:24,460 --> 01:12:26,416
- What?
- (Chuckles )

713
01:12:26,500 --> 01:12:28,456
Hey, Bobby, I wanna play this close,

714
01:12:28,540 --> 01:12:32,055
like we did with that other girl,
the one with the black hair.

715
01:12:32,140 --> 01:12:34,893
- It felt good, what do you think?
- That's good.

716
01:12:34,980 --> 01:12:37,448
Just don't rush that line again.

717
01:12:37,540 --> 01:12:40,850
I told you,
the line when you say, "Before what?"

718
01:12:41,740 --> 01:12:44,208
Bobby, acting is reacting.

719
01:12:44,300 --> 01:12:48,009
I just play off 'em.
They all say...um, uh...

720
01:12:48,100 --> 01:12:51,649
"They're gonna arrest you," like
that. "Then they'll put you in jail."

721
01:12:51,740 --> 01:12:54,538
They all say it the same way,
so I just react.

722
01:12:54,620 --> 01:12:56,451
- What's your name?
- Betty.

723
01:12:56,540 --> 01:12:59,771
Betty, you don't rush it,
I don't rush it.

724
01:12:59,860 --> 01:13:01,213
OK?

725
01:13:01,300 --> 01:13:04,053
Now, we're gonna play this
nice and close.

726
01:13:04,140 --> 01:13:06,290
Just like in the movies, OK?

727
01:13:08,940 --> 01:13:10,976
Dad's best friend goes to work.

728
01:13:12,540 --> 01:13:14,576
Bob?

729
01:13:16,340 --> 01:13:17,978
And...

730
01:13:18,940 --> 01:13:20,692
action.

731
01:13:23,740 --> 01:13:25,810
You're still here.

732
01:13:26,940 --> 01:13:28,896
I came back.

733
01:13:28,980 --> 01:13:30,936
I thought that's what you wanted.

734
01:13:31,020 --> 01:13:33,580
- Nobody wants you here.
- Really?

735
01:13:34,580 --> 01:13:36,536
My parents are right upstairs.

736
01:13:36,620 --> 01:13:40,090
- They think you've left.
- So surprise!

737
01:13:40,180 --> 01:13:42,136
I can call them.

738
01:13:42,220 --> 01:13:44,176
I can call my dad.

739
01:13:44,260 --> 01:13:46,216
But you won't.

740
01:14:01,100 --> 01:14:03,375
You're playing a dangerous game here.

741
01:14:05,100 --> 01:14:07,056
If you're trying to blackmail me,

742
01:14:08,060 --> 01:14:10,016
it's not gonna work.

743
01:14:11,540 --> 01:14:13,496
You know what I want.

744
01:14:13,580 --> 01:14:15,536
It's not that difficult.

745
01:14:19,060 --> 01:14:21,016
Get out.

746
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:24,889
Get out before I call my dad.

747
01:14:25,780 --> 01:14:27,736
He trusts you.

748
01:14:27,820 --> 01:14:29,572
You're his...

749
01:14:29,660 --> 01:14:31,571
best friend.

750
01:14:35,660 --> 01:14:38,174
This will be the end of everything.

751
01:14:40,260 --> 01:14:42,216
What about you?

752
01:14:42,300 --> 01:14:44,530
What'll your dad think about you?

753
01:14:44,620 --> 01:14:47,134
Stop.

754
01:14:47,220 --> 01:14:49,176
Stop it.

755
01:14:50,740 --> 01:14:53,493
That's what you said
from the beginning.

756
01:14:54,500 --> 01:14:58,573
If I tell them what happened they'll
arrest you and put you in jail.

757
01:15:05,660 --> 01:15:07,651
So get out of here.

758
01:15:07,740 --> 01:15:09,492
Before...

759
01:15:12,900 --> 01:15:14,856
Before what?

760
01:15:32,260 --> 01:15:33,978
Before...

761
01:15:35,060 --> 01:15:37,016
I kill you.

762
01:15:51,340 --> 01:15:53,649
Well, then they'd put you in jail.

763
01:16:02,140 --> 01:16:04,096
I hate you.

764
01:16:05,500 --> 01:16:07,456
I hate us both.

765
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:07,316
- I'm gonna take her over there.
- Yeah, big time.

766
00:00:10,884 --> 00:00:12,840
Well, there it was.

767
00:00:13,924 --> 00:00:15,960
Yeah, there it was all right.

768
00:00:16,044 --> 00:00:19,241
Baby, you got a way with you. Really.

769
00:00:19,324 --> 00:00:20,962
Bob?

770
00:00:22,044 --> 00:00:24,080
Very good.

771
00:00:24,164 --> 00:00:25,677
Really.

772
00:00:25,764 --> 00:00:28,483
I mean, it was forced, maybe, but...

773
00:00:28,564 --> 00:00:31,032
still humanistic.

774
00:00:31,124 --> 00:00:33,035
Yeah.

775
00:00:33,124 --> 00:00:35,558
(Bob ) Very good. Really.

776
00:00:35,644 --> 00:00:37,600
Really.

777
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,154
Oh, I thank you, Betty.

778
00:00:46,124 --> 00:00:48,115
I really mean that sincerely.

779
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:51,401
I mean, it was...extraordinary.

780
00:00:52,484 --> 00:00:54,440
You've done your aunt proud today.

781
00:00:54,524 --> 00:00:57,596
I am going to tell her that
first chance I get.

782
00:00:57,684 --> 00:00:59,242
Now,

783
00:00:59,324 --> 00:01:02,714
you and I are going to speak again
very soon.

784
00:01:02,804 --> 00:01:04,760
(Betty ) Thank you, Mr Brown.

785
00:01:04,844 --> 00:01:08,917
Thank you, Wally. I'm sure
you all have a lot to talk about.

786
00:01:09,004 --> 00:01:11,564
- We'll walk Betty out.
- Oh, well, yes, indeed.

787
00:01:11,644 --> 00:01:13,600
And it was our pleasure, Linney.

788
00:01:13,684 --> 00:01:16,437
Now, don't you
be a stranger around here.

789
00:01:16,524 --> 00:01:18,480
We love to have you here.

790
